<title>USA: FirstFed Q3 loan charge-offs $11.8 mln.</title>
<headline>FirstFed Q3 loan charge-offs $11.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>FirstFed Financial Corp on Friday reported that third quarter loan charge-offs had risen to $11.8 million, compared with $7.1 million for the year-ago quarter.</p>
<p>Loan charge-offs rose to $29.7 million for the nine-month period, compared with $18.0 million for the first nine months of 1995, the company said.</p>
<p>On Friday the company reported a third quarter loss of $0.49 per share including a one-time charge for the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
